## Create Compute Node Image

First, we create a minimal compute node image.  Warewulf supports using
container images as the base file system for provisioning, and it can import
these directly from an OCI registry like Docker Hub. Container images must be
created especially for use with Warewulf since they need to include things like
a kernel and an init system. {% if is_ubuntu -%}
In this example we will import the official Ubuntu container image, then install
the kernel and init-system packages needed for Warewulf provisioning.
{% else -%}
In this example we will import our base image from a set maintained by the
Warewulf community on the GitHub container registry.
{% endif %}

The `wwctl image exec` command runs the commands below it, these commands also
be run interactively one a time with the command `wwctl image shell {{ baseos
}}`. You can add `/bin/false` as the last command to prevent the image from
rebuilding (it will show an error) and rebuild later with the `wwctl image
build` command.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Create compute image for Warewulf -->
```bash
# Import the base image from Warewulf
{% if is_ubuntu -%}
wwctl image import docker://{{ distro_container_image }} \
	{{ baseos }} --syncuser
{% else -%}
wwctl image import docker://ghcr.io/warewulf/warewulf-{{ distro_container_image }} \
	{{ baseos }} --syncuser
{% endif -%}

# Define chroot location
CHROOT=$(wwctl image show {{ baseos }})
export CHROOT
```
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure HTTPS proxy for compute image (site-specific) -->
<!-- ohpc_command #<<< ohpc_proxy:compute >>># -->
```bash
# Enable OpenHPC inside image and update image.
# Disable image build on exit, rebuild later.
wwctl image exec --build=false {{ baseos }} -- /bin/bash -ex <<- EOF
{% if is_ubuntu %}
  apt update
  apt -y install ca-certificates curl systemd systemd-sysv \
    udev kmod linux-image-generic initramfs-tools network-manager openssh-server
  OHPC_REPO_ROOT="{{ ohpc_repo_server }}{{ ohpc_repo_path }}"
  OHPC_UBUNTU_REPO="\${OHPC_REPO_ROOT}/Ubuntu_24.04"
  OHPC_RELEASE_DEB="{{ ohpc_release_deb }}"
  curl -fsSLO "\${OHPC_UBUNTU_REPO}/all/\${OHPC_RELEASE_DEB}"
  apt -y install "./\${OHPC_RELEASE_DEB}"
  rm -f "\${OHPC_RELEASE_DEB}"
  apt update
  apt -y upgrade
{% else %}
  dnf -y install dnf-utils
  dnf -y install {{ ohpc_repo_server }}/OpenHPC/{{ ohpc_version_tree }}/{{ ostree }}/\
{{ arch }}/ohpc-release-{{ ohpc_version_tree }}-1.{{ distro_tag }}.{{ arch }}.rpm
  dnf -y update
{% endif %}
EOF
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
